WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.556
Scenario: Ransomware encrypted production servers. An offline backup exists, but

2
00:00:05.556 --> 00:00:11.111
it has not been validated; credentials may be exposed. Safest

3
00:00:11.111 --> 00:00:16.667
response: validate clean backups, establish a trusted recovery environment, remediate

4
00:00:16.667 --> 00:00:22.222
identities, restore prioritized services, test and monitor. Option B is

5
00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:27.778
unsafe because The newest backup may also be encrypted, compromised

6
00:00:27.778 --> 00:00:33.333
or contaminated. Option C is unsafe because Payment does not

7
00:00:33.333 --> 00:00:38.889
guarantee decryption, recovery or prevention of data disclosure. Option D

8
00:00:38.889 --> 00:00:44.444
is unsafe because Stopped encryption does not prove attacker access

9
00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:50.000
or persistence is gone. In practice: follow the recovery plan

10
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.556
and confirm integrity and security before return to service. Key

11
00:00:55.556 --> 00:01:00.000
takeaway: restore only to a known-good, monitored state.

